      "writtenOn": "2026-07-14T18:13:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the rust reader holds a raw pointer to the stream.  Not sure if it\u0027s truly problematic to destroy them out of order, but it\u0027d be safer to reverse the declaration order and avoid any dangling pointer issues.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 90,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 92,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "dcd6208b529ab94650e30bd2ae8e2a88567c34c0",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "896375f8_72ffca88",
        "filename": "experimental/rust_jpeg/decoder/impl/SkJpegRustCodec.h",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 92,
      "author": {
        "id": 4159917
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-16T20:14:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good catch. I reversed the member declaration/initialization order so the stream outlives the Rust reader during destruction. The Rust reader can indirectly reference the stream adapter, so this avoids any dangling-pointer risk from member teardown order.",
      "parentUuid": "4dfd15cc_581c13c9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 90,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 92,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "dcd6208b529ab94650e30bd2ae8e2a88567c34c0",
